{
    "background_story": "Arturo was a skilled stonemason who spent his days working on the grand cathedral in the city's center. He took great pride in his craft, carefully shaping each stone to fit perfectly into the intricate design. One fateful day, while working high above the ground, a stone suddenly began to spall, cracking and breaking apart in his hands. Arturo's quick reflexes allowed him to dodge the falling debris, but he knew the incident could have been disastrous. Undeterred, he used the experience as an opportunity to develop a new technique for reinforcing the stones, making the cathedral's structure even more resilient. His innovative solution earned him recognition among his peers, and Arturo's work became a benchmark for stonemasons across the land.",
